.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt SDL1-JSTEST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sdl1-jstest
.Nd test joysticks through SDL 1.2
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f | w
.Op Fl Fl geometry Ar W Ns x Ns Ar H
.Op Fl Fl data-dir Ar dir
.Op Ar mode
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the joysticks SDL 1.2 detects, their axes, buttons, hats and balls,
and displays their state or the events they send, the way programs
built with SDL 1.2 see them, instead of reading the raw
.Pa /dev/input
devices.
.Pp
Without a mode option
.Nm
opens a device menu: in the terminal when built with ncurses,
otherwise in a window.
.Ss Modes
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l , Fl Fl list
List the joysticks and their properties.
.It Fl t Ar JOYNUM , Fl Fl test Ar JOYNUM
Show the state of joystick
.Ar JOYNUM
in the terminal (ncurses builds; otherwise the same as
.Fl Fl gui ) .
.It Fl G , Fl Fl gui Op Ar JOYNUM
Show the device menu in a window, or with
.Ar JOYNUM
that device's state; leaving its view then ends the program.
.It Fl e Ar JOYNUM , Fl Fl event Ar JOYNUM
Print the events received from the joystick until interrupted.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl v , Fl Fl version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl Fl show-paths
Print the data directory and where it was found, then exit.
.El
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl data-dir Ar dir
Use
.Ar dir
as the data directory (sdl1-jstest reads no data; the option exists
for symmetry with its siblings).
.It Fl f , Fl Fl fullscreen
Open the window fullscreen.
.It Fl w , Fl Fl windowed
Open the window windowed (the default).
.It Fl Fl geometry Ar W Ns x Ns Ar H
Window size; the default is 640x480.
The display is scaled to the window with its aspect ratio kept.
.El
.Sh WINDOW CONTROLS
In the menu, the arrow keys move, Enter opens a device and Esc quits;
a mouse click or a tap opens a row, the last row quits.
On a joystick the stick or hat moves, pressing a button steps to the
next row and holding a button for one second opens the selected one.
.Pp
A device view is left with Esc, the
.Dq Menu
button at the top right, or by holding any button for two seconds.
Ctrl-C quits everywhere.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SDL_VIDEODRIVER
The video driver.
Without a usable display the terminal modes fall back to
.Dq dummy .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when SDL or the window cannot be initialised, 2 on
invalid command line options.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
At startup
.Nm
prints a report to standard error: version, build, system, SDL
environment variables, the SDL library in use, the video and renderer
drivers and every joystick
found.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jstest 1 ,
.Xr jstest-gtk 1 ,
.Xr sdl2-jstest 1 ,
.Xr sdl3-jstest 1
